WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.520
A Shinobi, his young master

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.520
and the man who separates them...

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.740
this is how Sekiro begins.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.860
Busshi: "So you're awake..."

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.580
"Looks like death is not your fate...just yet."

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.720
The old man speaking is named Busshi,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.120
who is a hermit in an abandoned temple.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.920
While the player-character was unconscious,

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.280
the teaser trailer for Shadows Die Twice took place,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.580
and Busshi fashioned for us a new limb.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.300
This prosthetic arm is called "Ningishu".

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.440
Or as the hermit puts it

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.380
the perfect fangs for a one-armed wolf.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:45.580
Busshi: "You'll learn to appreciate its worth".

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.180
And so we're aptly named "Sekiro"

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.660
the wolf who is one half of a pair.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.680
It's really clever wordplay

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.300
as the missing half of a pair

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.420
could be referring to the arm we lost

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.120
But it could also be referring to the young lord

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.560
that was taken from us in the beginning

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.360
in both senses of the word

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.780
We play as a character who is defined by his missing half...

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.020
so I felt it's only fitting that we split this video in two:

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.520
just like the name Sekiro,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.300
one video for the story of our missing Lord,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.040
and one video for the gameplay Implications

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.640
of our prosthetic arm,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.320
because this arm can be fitted with many different attachments

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.320
and we know of five so far.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.640
So first: the axe.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.660
It's thrown into our own hand here

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.180
to crush the guards of shield-bearing enemies, 
you know,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.100
just like in Dark Souls 3,

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.100
leaving them open to a critical strike.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.660
But our second attachment

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.900
the one after this is far more innovative

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.880
It's a grappling hook

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.280
and if I had to guess

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.680
I bet we lock on to available roofs and ledges with R3

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.780
You know, just like we lock on to enemies

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.140
because later in the trailer

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.420
We see the character lock onto an enemy and

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.740
do a grappling hook attack onto them as well

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.760
So as game-changing as it is to grappling hook an enemy

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.900
and dash onto them

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.820
it has even more implications

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.840
when you think about level design

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.880
because it opens up this level of verticality to the maps

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.780
that we've literally never experienced in 'Souls' before

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.320
It's gonna be so sick,

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.860
because when you think about it

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.920
'Souls' is really limited by ladders and fall damage

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.640
But  in the time it takes you

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.640
to climb a ladder in Dark Souls,

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.120
you would have already scaled that height in Sekiro

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.940
and had extra time left over to leap off of the ledge,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.020
ambushing an enemy far below all in the blink of an eye.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.960
So just really huge gameplay implications there

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.460
but moving on.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.380
The third attachment has us

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.380
swiftly unsheath a steel conical hat

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.500
as a sort of emergency temporary shield.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.280
This implies that some attacks can't be deflected

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:50.180
with our sword

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.660
and we'll talk a little bit about that later.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.280
But the fourth attachment you might have missed:

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.220
you see it when our character scatters small fireworks before the horse

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.320
startling it

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.880
a better angle of this move is

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.880
actually seen in this screenshot here

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.060
where you can actually see the firecracker blinding an enemy.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.400
And finally, the fifth attachment.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.200
It's not actually seen in the trailer

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.520
but I doubt anyone's gonna be surprised

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.520
by what this cannon attachment does.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.560
It reminds me a lot of

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.860
Guts' hand cannon arm from 'Berserk' actually,

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.400
and thinking about this prosthetic arm,

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.840
it is good to know that they're still going strong

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.680
with their 'Berserk' inspiration.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.520
So if it isn't blatantly obvious already

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.680
Sekiro is clearly 'Souls-like'

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.280
it's surely the game that Miyazaki said

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.220
would 'comply with the expectations of fans

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.740
in a straightforward manner'.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.800
It has all the tell-tale signs,

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.600
it's got a nameless protagonist

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.240
for character customization;

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.360
it has an emphasis on difficulty that kills you;

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.460
and it also has combat that's been tweaked

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.420
just enough to make it distinct from other titles.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.100
And I think I've figured out what makes it largely distinct

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.440
from Souls and Bloodborne

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.600
(although I could be wrong)

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.280
but, think about Bloodborne for example:

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.960
what's at the core of its combat?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.020
It's the insanely quick dash ability.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.080
And what about Dark Souls?

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.040
Well at the core of its combat for most players is

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.880
the fact that its shields

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.880
can block the majority of damage.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.140
And then look at Sekiro:

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.860
the dash is certainly slower than in Bloodborne and

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.640
and Samurai were

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.720
that they were abandoning the shield matter

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.640
around that point in history.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.880
So what's left

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.160
is swordplay:

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.420
deflection, counter-attacks and

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.180
the concept of giving no ground to your opponent.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.260
The trailer has tons of examples of this

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.400
and I've actually never seen a Souls-borne gameplay trailer

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.100
with so much parrying,

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.620
which to me is evidence that we're going to be experiencing

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.120
a sort of swordplay that is on a higher level

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.860
than in previous titles.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.620
And it's really likely, I think, that the swordplay is

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:56.400
enhanced with the ability to use specific attack moves

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.940
almost as if you would use a spell or a weapon art in Dark Souls

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.660
So we'll talk a bit more about that now.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.700
Notice how the player's sword glints in certain moments.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.740
And have you noticed that red ancient Japanese text

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:11.900
seen here:

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.600
and off to the side here as well?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.460
So it's totally up for debate what these mean,

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.800
but I feel like they indicate that

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.140
our character might have access to

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.360
special abilities, skills and attacks,

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.500
some of which might only be possible

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.960
by a successful deflection or two,

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.620
because he only ever uses them

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.900
after he deflects an attack twice.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.800
And the opponent's we face

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.500
are just as capable of this as we are:

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.600
notice how the opponent's sword glints

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.940
right before he attempts this:

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.400
this double-handed dive attack onto the player

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.340
and this attack is coupled with a red symbol,

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:53.240
which you can see is generated from his character,

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.240
not ours.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.640
So it's difficult to identify what this character says

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:01.380
but the symbol seems to serve as a visual warning

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.040
and it looks a lot like

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.580
an ancient Japanese symbol for 'danger'.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.080
And I could be wrong,

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.000
but I believe that it's an alert

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.040
to sort of help you in fast-paced combat,

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.940
to assist you in recognizing

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.900
when you're about to be hit by a special attack,

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.100
and these attacks

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.080
might have to be blocked with this special hat shield,

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.320
or dodged, as the same symbol

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.220
appears here in the fight with the horseman

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.340
and the player dodges it there in response.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:29.900
For those with a keen eye,

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:30.940
you would have noticed that

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.220
another of these symbols actually goes off

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.720
in the trailer when the player is resurrected.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.200
It seems that he really does have to die twice,

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.260
and it's almost as if this passive resurrection ability is

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.800
activating along with this symbol.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:46.980
In this situation,

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.240
what I'm pretty sure is going down is

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.680
the enemy believes that Sekiro is dead

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.000
and Sekiro, the one-armed wolf,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.680
capitalizes on this, running really low

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.000
and stealthy behind the giant,

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.200
finishing him off with

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.480
what seems to be a a back-stab attack.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.120
And it's easy to look past this

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.320
but look at the way that he's running here

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.720
and here as well.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.580
Look at him crouching below these floorboards

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.940
and skirting this wall to avoid detection.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.060
To me,

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:17.180
it seems clear that there is a stealth ability in the game

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.260
so this absolutely fits in with the ninja flavor of the game

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.460
and just think about it

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.580
if you had some sort of way of looking around corners

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:27.980
this could enable amazing stealth gameplay.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:32.480
One of the tag-lines of the game is 'kill ingeniously',

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.840
so here's hoping they let us.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.120
I mean this guy definitely has his strategy sorted!

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.120
I guess that's...one way to apply pine resin!

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:43.560
Actually a few Chinese historical dramas

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.480
have depicted their executioners

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.340
coating their blade like this before a kill,

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.020
although it's difficult to identify exactly why they do this.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.680
So it's at this point

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.140
we definitely need to address a few leaks

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.820
that dropped a few weeks ago.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.880
Before this game was even revealed as 'Sekiro' at E3,

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.880
a lot of what leaked

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.460
actually ended up being in this trailer.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.740
Mainly the interaction between the main character

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.060
and the Hermit who gives him a new arm.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.500
So the fact that the leaks got this right

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.540
obviously lends credence to
 the rest of what they go on to say:

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:22.040
for example before we talked about abilities

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:24.420
and I talked about them a bit more confidently

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.900
because the leak suggested

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.680
that the diverse abilities existed in the game

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:31.760
outside of just traditional weapon movesets.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.800
The leak also suggested that

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.940
the game mostly takes place in rural locations

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.540
which seems to be the case from the trailer.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.760
But it also suggested that there is a larger city to explore as well

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.480
One question I have:

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.580
how are we supposed to travel between cities ?

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.580
Please tell me that we can travel

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:52.300
and fight on horseback!

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.260
And while people are currently freaking out

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.700
that the game won't be Multiplayer at all,

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:01.680
the leak suggests that the game will at least have a unique PvP system,

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.160
where you sort of enter the world of someone else

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.780
under the guise of an enemy

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:10.100
and you take control of that  enemy within the level

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.300
with enhanced abilities.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.700
So from the enemies we've seen, that could be

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.100
this Samurai

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.820
the horseman

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:20.200
or even the huge murakumo wielder.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.980
I can see that happening.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:25.840
From memory, this was also supposed to be a mechanic in Bloodborne,

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:29.680
where you invaded other people's worlds as a more traditional beast,

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.600
but it was scrapped.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:38.060
Sekiro also supposedly features a day-and-night/dynamic weather system,

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.760
which was itself supposed to make it into Dark Souls 3,

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:45.380
and to this day there's still code in Dark Souls 3

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.880
that shows evidence of a day-and-night cycle.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.840
One can only hope that with Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:55.380
they get to deliver the full brunt of their ambitions with this game,

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.440
and this is kind of the perfect time to talk about it...

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.380
the elephant in the room, and the company

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:04.380
that will allow them to maybe fulfill all of their ambitions:

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:05.480
Activision.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:10.040
Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice is published by Activision

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.180
Not NAMCO BANDAI or Sony as before.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.540
I don't think anyone saw this coming:

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.560
my first thought when seeing this was relief,

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.220
absolute relief.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:21.780
First because this meant

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.780
Shadows Die Twice wasn't going to be

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.580
a PS4 exclusive title as expected,

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:27.980
which is great

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.980
because console exclusives suck.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.260
They're really bad for consumers:

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.680
they pointlessly limit the amount of people

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.200
who can enjoy these amazing games, and

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:40.880
not to mention being able to have this game on PC

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.560
does wonders for the YouTube community.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.220
For me, for example,

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.240
it allows me to make better-looking videos

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:50.920
It allows me to make them faster with amazing camera angles

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.760
and way more creativity.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.200
I was also relieved

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.860
because publishing through Activision meant that

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.960
this game was a new IP

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:02.480
and From Software thrives with new IPs, everyone knows that,

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.680
look at Demon Souls and Dark Souls 1 and Bloodborne.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.880
The universe that From Software crafts

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:10.680
in the first episode of a franchise is

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:13.820
always more exciting than their attempts to

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.640
sort of build on existing stories

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.220
and inevitably recycle elements of them.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:22.340
So if From Software is happy with the amount of money

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.800
that Activision is throwing at their project

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.800
then I'm happy with it too.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:30.520
I mean, I will be really, really wary of

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.140
any hint of casualization or

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.200
monetization going forward

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.780
but I seriously doubt that

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:40.060
From Software would compromise on those values now of all times.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.680
Because, think about it,

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.460
From Software is courting at least three publishers here.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.100
They are courting NAMCO,

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.500
they're courting Activision,

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.080
they're courting Sony,

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.240
and games under Miyazaki

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:54.080
have delivered time and time again.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:56.960
So if you're a developer in a position to

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.840
court three publishers for the best deal,

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:03.420
there's a pretty good chance they got the best deal

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.420
so good for them, I guess!

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.220
Now I kind of just want to know

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.920
if they'll put it on the Blizzard launcher!

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.760
So, to sum up: what don't we know about the gameplay?

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.520
We don't know what the in-game currency is,

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.220
considering there's no souls or blood echoes,

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.660
and I have no clue

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.940
what's going to be used as a checkpoint marker

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.940
without bonfires or a dream.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:27.500
We don't know how to invest in our own character or level up,

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.420
nor do we know how exactly

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.480
Sekiro keeps coming back to life

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.220
In fact, I wouldn't be surprised

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:37.840
if they rethought the entire death mechanic a little bit.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.900
The way he comes to life mid-combat

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.840
made me wonder if you could design 'Souls'

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.480
without checkpoints,

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.760
or true death,

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:51.260
just the ability to keep on getting up somehow and persist.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.720
Anyway, what we do know is

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:56.920
there is a hell of a lot of story, already, like seriously

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.840
there's a lot on the Japanese website

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.140
that we've translated,

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:01.720
and I'll see you in part 2 for that

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.300
because it sounds like a fascinating world

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.780
and I can't wait to tell you why.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.780
So thanks for watching guys and take it easy!

